  "chain": "cracked 1977 yoke weld [cause B] -> actuator flexes away from valve body, stroke length increases -> potentiometer over-ranges into dead-band -> downstream open-permissive relay stays open -> HX 'A' Tube Side Discharge Valve fails to open from MCR -> (parallel: Division II LPCI breakers racked for test) -> both divisions of Suppression Pool Cooling/Spray/Drywell Spray inoperable for 3h39m [no operable ECCS backup asserted; Division I LPCI capable of feeding sprays but CCSW-cooled spray function itself was the lost function]",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Root cause is design/manufacturing/installation (cause code B) tied to a 1977 weld defect; the potentiometer over-range and relay failure are proximate mechanical/electrical consequences, not independently caused failure origins, so the chain is linear rather than parallel except for the coincident Division II breaker test outage, which is a separate contemporaneous failure mode leading to the same consequence. No BACKED_UP_BY edge asserted because no system is stated to have remained operable to replace the lost CCSW-cooled containment spray/suppression pool cooling function during the 3h39m window (Division I LPCI could feed sprays but without CCSW cooling, per narrative, so it does not constitute a full backup of the lost safety function). Five previous occurrences referenced only by date, not LER number, in the narrative; stub keys are placeholders built from date since no formal LER numbers were given in text."
}